  "id": "Compound::DB08798 - Gene::1559",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Sulfamoxole may interact with Cyp2c9 through a mechanism involving structural similarity and binding. Sulfamoxole is classified as a sulfonamide anti-infective agent, and it shares structural similarities with sulfacytine and sulfadimethoxine, both of which bind to Cyp2c9. This indicates a potential for Sulfamoxole to exert its effects via a similar binding mechanism. Additionally, Sulfamoxole is related to silver sulfadiazine, which also binds to Cyp2c9, further supporting the possibility of a shared interaction pathway. The evidence is consistent with a mechanism where structural resemblance leads to binding, and the lowest common ancestors of the related compounds all fall under the broader category of sulfonamide anti-infective agents or sulfonamides. The strength of the evidence is supported by multiple paths with high scores, but the exact nature of the interaction remains inferred due to the lack of direct experimental data.",
